# R5 risky surfaces for claude-code-fleet-notify — a PR touching ANY of these
# requires both adversarial auditors (audit/grok + audit/gatekeeper) to post a
# success commit status before it can merge (enforced by r5-audit-gate.yml).
#
# DESIGN: broad default-covering GLOBS, NOT a drift-prone allowlist. (Gatekeeper
# PR#25 BLOCK: the first port enumerated scripts/ — exactly the allowlist trap —
# missing the 10 fleet CLIs incl taey-notify, and missed root-level identity.py
# which every hook imports. Over-gate trivial changes > under-gate a blast surface.)
#
# The hook layer — a bad hook command disabled every tool on the machine once
# (the 2026-06-11 outage); changes here drive every session:
hooks/*.py
# identity.py — top-level module imported by EVERY hook; part of the import
# closure behind that same outage (PR#18). Root-level, so not under hooks/*.
identity.py
# The delivery library (inbox/daemon/handoff/trace):
notifications/*.py
# ALL scripts — the installer (the outage came through it), the daemon, the
# deploy, AND the fleet CLIs (taey-notify is the inter-session messaging
# backbone the whole fleet runs on). Glob, not an enumerated list:
scripts/*
# CI / gate config itself (self-protecting):
.github/workflows/*.yml
.github/r5-risky-paths
# Packaging:
setup.py
